{"name":"Corselette","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Corselette_gossard1953.jpg/960px-Corselette_gossard1953.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corselette_gossard1953.jpg","caption":"Corselette gossard1953","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["A corselette is a women's foundation garment that joins a bra and a girdle in one piece, with shoulder straps and a body extending to the top of the thighs. It lifts the bust and smooths the torso under clothes.\nIt became popular in 1914 as an alternative to wearing a bra with a girdle or corset, and styles include open versions with suspenders and panty versions. Its shaping lasts only while worn."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["It is worn under clothing in place of a separate bra and girdle. Boning or wires support the cups and keep strapless versions in place; some designs use panels of non-stretch fabric through the front to flatten and shape."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["No specific risks are documented beyond general discomfort associated with compressive garments."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Corselette_gossard1953.jpg/960px-Corselette_gossard1953.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a8/Corselette_gossard1953.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Corselette gossard1953","license":"Public domain","creator":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corselette_gossard1953.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Corselette_%28AM_1997.34.6-3%29.jpg/960px-Corselette_%28AM_1997.34.6-3%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campa