://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f9/Corselette_%28AM_2000.93.160-5%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Corselette (AM 2000.93.160-5)","license":"CC BY 4.0","creator":"Bendon; Berlei","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corselette_(AM_2000.93.160-5).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Corselette_%28AM_2000.93.160-7%29.jpg/960px-Corselette_%28AM_2000.93.160-7%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6e/Corselette_%28AM_2000.93.160-7%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Corselette (AM 2000.93.160-7)","license":"CC BY 4.0","creator":"Bendon; Berlei","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corselette_(AM_2000.93.160-7).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Corselette_%28AM_2000.93.160-1%29.jpg/960px-Corselette_%28AM_2000.93.160-1%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/ba/Corselette_%28AM_2000.93.160-1%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Corselette (AM 2000.93.160-1)","license":"CC BY 4.0","creator":"Bendon; Berlei","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corselette_(AM_2000.93.160-1).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Corselette_%28AM_2000.93.160-2%29.jpg/960px-Corselette_%28AM_2000.93.160-2%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ee/Corselette_%28AM_2000.93.160-2%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Corselette (AM 2000.93.160-2)","license":"CC BY 4.0","creator":"Bendon; Berlei","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corselette_(AM_2000.93.160-2).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/7388cec1-eff0-4c69-8747-6149fc679c01/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/2566/4187067537_c71a30a8f0_b.jpg","title":"1966 corselette or shaper","license":"BY-NC 2.0","creator":"genibee","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/21233184@N02/4187067537","source":"Flickr"}],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Pantie-corselette","url":"https://europepmc.org/article/PAT/CN2760990Y","source":null,"year":2006,"cites":0,"kind":null}],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Corselette - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corselette"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Physique","chain":["One-piece garment supports bust","Girdle section compresses waist and hips","Smoother, more defined silhouette while worn"],"effect":"direct","text":"The garment shapes the body under clothes by lifting the bust and compressing the midsection. The effect lasts only while it is worn."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["A corselette is a women's foundation garment combining a bra and a girdle, with shoulder straps and a body that extends down to around the top of the legs; it can include lace and be open-style with suspenders or panty-style [1].","It supports the bust and controls the waist and hips so that clothing sits smoothly. A Chinese utility model patent for a siamesed panty-corselette describes design aims of supporting the chest and thinning the waist, using a non-stretch central panel [2]."],"infobox":[["Type","Foundation garment (bra + girdle)"],["Popularized","1914"],["Notable design","Warner's Merry Widow, 1952"],["Styles","Open with suspenders; panty-style"]],"sections":[{"h":"History","paras":["The word likely derives from corset plus the diminutive -ette; the older corselet named a piece of plate armor [1]. The corselette became popular in 1914 as a single-piece alternative to a separate bra and girdle or corset [1]. Bust uplift cups appeared in 1933 but became common from 1943, and in 1952 Warner's released the Merry Widow, which used elastic netting, a zipper and nine spiral wires [1]. From around 1960, tights and trousers began replacing corselettes [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Design","paras":["Boning supports the cup section and helps strapless versions stay up [1]. Modern designs, such as the patented siamesed panty-corselette, combine a front panel, back panel, legs and shoulder straps with a central non-stretch zone intended to support the chest and thin the waist [2]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1914","event":"Corselettes become popular as a one-piece alternative to bra plus girdle [1]."},{"year":"1933","event":"Bust uplift cups appear [1]."},{"year":"1952","event":"Warner's releases the Merry Widow [1]."},{"year":"1960","event":"Tights and trousers begin replacing corselettes [1]."}],"refs":[{"title":"Corselette","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corselette","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Pantie-corselette","url":"https://europepmc.org/article/PAT/CN2760990Y","source":"Patent CN2760990Y","year":2006,"type":"study"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[]}